A||||8||William Federle||1984 SE clutch||||1||
Z||000000||William Federle||01-11-2000||06:51 PM||||Sometime within the first 3 minutes or so after I start my Fiero and begin driving, especially if it is cold, I hear a screeching sound that is worse when it is colder. It goes away in 10-15 seconds. When it is warm 40 deg F or so, it doesn't seem to happen. Is this the throwout bearing? The clutch works ok - it doesn't seem to be slipping. Has this happened to anyone else?||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||01-11-2000||06:57 PM||||The description sounds like the alternator belt. What makes you think clutch? Does it only do it when the clutch is in?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||William Federle||01-11-2000||07:11 PM||||I guess I figured that the alternator belt would keep on screeching - this stops like I said after 10-15 sec. Maybe I'll try a new belt. I sure hope that's it. Thanks for the reply.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||01-11-2000||07:18 PM||||I've had several cars that the belt only slipped for the first little bit and were worse when cold. Maybe a higher load to recharge battery after starting??? Belt may just need tightened... Good Luck.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJRice||01-12-2000||08:36 AM||||My brother's 86 SE V6 does the same thing, and after much playing with the belts, we decided that what we were hearing was actually air being sucked into the system quickly.  Check your vacuum hoses to make sure that you dont have any off/loose/rotted.<P>This is a shot in the dark, but that was the source of all the noise in my brothers car.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ggarsk||01-12-2000||10:37 AM||||My '84 did the same thing...just tighten or better yet replace your belt. That will fix the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000006||William Federle||01-12-2000||10:55 AM||||I just ran up to Advance auto and got a new belt - the only thing is it's one of those cogged belts - I think that they're noisier than the old style belts. Well, at least it's new. I'll put it on tonight when I get home and by this time tomorrow I'll know if that's it. <P>I think I'm going to replace all of those plastic vacuum lines with regular rubber ones.<P>Thanks to all who replied.||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||01-12-2000||05:03 PM||||If you want to know if it is the belt just spray the belt with some WD-40 or anything while it is making the noise. If the noise stops when you do this, it's the belt. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||William Federle||01-13-2000||07:09 PM||||It must have been the belt. I put it on last night and this morning before work and this afternoon after work there was no screeching noise - it was about 15 deg. F both times.||||reg||1
